From de4111cfc3d835438b7c5ee3b558d71f0ccbc7e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 15:48:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] samples/bpf: add XDP RPS/RFS steering sample

Add an XDP sample that demonstrates receive packet steering with a
CPUMAP-backed data path. The sample parses IPv4/IPv6 TCP and UDP flows,
uses a hash-selected RPS CPU when no flow affinity is known, and redirects
packets through a configured CPUMAP.

Add an RFS state table that tracks active and desired CPUs per flow. TCP
sockops callbacks and an explicit tcp_recvmsg kprobe can record userspace
CPU hints and update the desired CPU. The kprobe path refreshes the hint on
each receive so process migration is reflected after connection setup.

Support three RFS CPU selection strategies: use the process CPU, choose an
alternate CPU from the same cluster, or choose an alternate CPU from the
same NUMA node. Topology is read in userspace and precomputed into simple
maps for verifier-friendly BPF lookups.

Preserve packet ordering during CPU migration by tracking CPUMAP enqueue
and dequeue progress. XDP keeps using the old active CPU until the old CPU
queue has drained past the saved tail value, then commits the desired CPU
as active.

Also add pinned map operations for manual flow updates, statistics,
and flow state inspection.

Developed with assistance from Codex:GPT-5.

Tested with:
  make M=samples/bpf xdp_rps_rfs_user.o xdp_rps_rfs_kern.o \
    CLANG=clang-18 LLC=llc-18 OPT=opt-18 LLVM_DIS=llvm-dis-18 \
    LLVM_OBJCOPY=llvm-objcopy-18 LLVM_READELF=llvm-readelf-18 -j$(nproc)
  scripts/checkpatch.pl --strict --no-tree -f \
    samples/bpf/xdp_rps_rfs_kern.c samples/bpf/xdp_rps_rfs_user.c
  test-kernel arch/x86/boot/bzImage
  /mnt/shared/bpf_rfs_numa_test.sh
